            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Description of a clinical case of enteropathic arthritis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">Descriptive study. SITE. Health Centre.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PATIENTS AND OTHER PARTICIPANTS" NlmCategory="METHODS">A clinical case is described, starting with back pain where X-rays perceive no irregularity. Later a diagnosis of Crohn's disease is made. Finally lesions characteristic of anchylo-poyethic spondylitis appear.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INTERVENTIONS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Corticosteroid treatment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MEASUREMENTS AND MAIN FINDINGS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Clinical investigations and complementary diagnoses.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Way in which spondylitis presents, with no clear X-ray indications. Importance of closely following the development of this type of patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
